{"id":"daberath","name":"Daberath","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:daberath"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Daberath","text":"Pasture, a Levitical town of Issachar (Josh. 19:12; 21:28), near the border of Zebulum. It is the modern small village of Deburich, at the base of Mount Tabor. Tradition has incorrectly made it the scene of the miracle of the cure of the lunatic child (Matt. 17:14)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H1705","lemma":"דֲּבְרַת","xlit":"Dăbrath","gloss":"Daberath, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Dabareh, Daberath","count":3,"share":1},{"strong":"H3485","lemma":"יִשָּׂשכָר","xlit":"Yissâˢkâr","gloss":"Jissaskar, a son of Jacob","kjv":"Issachar","count":2,"share":0.67},{"strong":"H4054","lemma":"מִגְרָשׁ","xlit":"migrâsh","gloss":"a suburb","kjv":"cast out, suburb","count":2,"share":0.67},{"strong":"H4294","lemma":"מַטֶּה","xlit":"maṭṭeh","gloss":"a branch","kjv":"rod, staff, tribe","count":2,"share":0.67}],"verses":["Josh.19.12","Josh.21.28","1Chr.6.72"],"related":[{"id":"issachar","type":"lexical","strong":"H3485","why":"both lead with יִשָּׂשכָר (H3485)"},{"id":"issachar-the-tribe-of","type":"lexical","strong":"H3485","why":"both lead with יִשָּׂשכָר (H3485)"}],"works":[]}
